From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 13:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qcs6490-rubikpi3: enable AP6256 SDIO WiFi
Upstream-Status: Pending

The Thundercomm Rubik Pi 3 has an Ampak AP6256 module (Broadcom BCM43456
WiFi + BCM4345C5 BT) wired to SDIO via sdhc_2 and UART7. The BT side is
already described in the mainline DTS, but the WiFi side has no SDIO
child node, so brcmfmac never sees the chip.

Add a wifi@1 child under &sdhc_2 with compatible "brcm,bcm4329-fmac" (the
catch-all binding all brcmfmac SDIO parts use; the actual chip ID is
auto-discovered during probe). The host-wake interrupt is wired to TLMM
GPIO 38, pinmux already defined as wifi_host_wake. Power rails come from
the existing always-on vreg_wifi_1v8.

Pair with brcmfmac43456-sdio.bin from rubikpi-ai/rubikpi3-firmware
(renamed from fw_bcm43456c5_ag.bin) and the board-specific NVRAM at
brcmfmac43456-sdio.thundercomm,rubikpi3.txt.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-thundercomm-rubikpi3.dts | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-thundercomm-rubikpi3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-thundercomm-rubikpi3.dts
index abcdef123456..abcdef123457 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-thundercomm-rubikpi3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-thundercomm-rubikpi3.dts
@@ -1000,11 +1000,25 @@
 	vmmc-supply = <&vreg_l9c_2p96>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vreg_l6c_2p96>;

+	bus-width = <4>;
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <0>;
+
 	non-removable;
 	keep-power-in-suspend;
 	/delete-property/ cd-gpios;

 	status = "okay";
+
+	wifi@1 {
+		compatible = "brcm,bcm4329-fmac";
+		reg = <1>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&tlmm>;
+		interrupts = <38 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		interrupt-names = "host-wake";
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&wifi_host_wake>;
+	};
 };

 /* Pin 19, 21, 23, 24 in 40-pin connector */

--
